# Contributing to Rocci

Rocci is an experimental preview. **We do not accept pull requests at this
point.** That may change in the near future. The repository
[CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/koliyo/rocci/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)
is the full contract. This page is a short map.

## Getting started

1. Clone `https://github.com/koliyo/rocci` and work on a named branch.
2. Use Rust 1.85+, `roc` and `cargo` on `PATH`, and the Wry platform packages
   from [Install](/docs/install/).
3. Run `cargo test --workspace` and `cargo fmt --all -- --check`.

## Ownership layers

Change the owning crate. The same table lives in
[AGENTS.md](https://github.com/koliyo/rocci/blob/main/AGENTS.md).

- `.rocci` grammar, lowering, or source maps: `crates/rocci-template`
- Markdown, Rocdown declarations, site catalog, and generator: `crates/rocci-rocdown`
- Shared runtime configuration: `crates/rocci-core`
- Application documentation staging: `crates/rocci-docs`
- CLI template build, run, preview, or bundle: `crates/rocci-cli` and `crates/rocci-desktop`
- CLI document and site build, run, check, or test: `crates/rocci-rocdown-cli`
- Portable OKF parsing, validation, search, and artifacts: `crates/okf`
- Knowledge review CLI and bundle tools: `crates/rocci-okf`
- Shared UI primitives: `crates/rocci-ui`
- Documentation site chrome: `crates/rocci-rocdown/templates/RocdownTheme.rocci`
- rocci.dev document shell: `site/theme/`
- Editors: `crates/rocci-lsp`, `crates/rocci-rocdown-lsp`, `editors/vscode`, `editors/zed`
- Syntax highlighting grammars: `crates/rocci-highlight`

## Code conventions

- Keep parsing loops monotonic so malformed input cannot hang.
- Add regression tests in the narrowest owning crate.
- Public contracts belong in crate READMEs and `/docs/`, not in archived
  reports.

## Pull requests and CI

Do not open a pull request expecting review or a merge. Maintainer and
Dependabot PRs do not start GitHub Actions automatically. After review, a
maintainer comments `/ci` to run hosted CI and Knowledge on the PR head.
Dependabot PRs need the same `/ci` comment. Do not run `/ci-local` on
external or Dependabot pull requests; that command is reserved for
`koliyo` same-repository work (`/cl-local` is an alias).

